      "budget_share": 0.45,
      "why": "The 50 MSPS throughput constraint rules out iterative/unrolled_k (they emit one result every several cycles, so they need Fmax >> 50 MHz, inflating power). pipelined_m is the key family: it gives 1 result/cycle like pipelined, but by registering every m stages it cuts FF count and area (hence power_index) while keeping the same bit-accurate result. m is the main power/area lever, so I sweep it fully (2..8). data_width 14..18 and n_iter 12..16 bracket the accuracy target (max_abs_err <= 2^-12) with headroom to map the power-vs-accuracy trade-off; angle_guard/frac_guard kept small to avoid area bloat. This is where the interesting Pareto trade-off lives."
    },
