        {"param": "rounding", "low": null, "high": null, "choices": ["trunc", "round"]}
      ],
      "budget_share": 0.35,
      "why": "The full pipelined family (m=1) is the throughput-safe baseline and the upper bound on FF/area/power for a given accuracy. Including it anchors the high-accuracy/high-power end of the front and lets the hypervolume capture the full trade-off curve, not just the m>1 corner. Same accuracy-relevant ranges as pipelined_m so the two families are directly comparable on the accuracy axis."
    },
